# Form-Native JIT Track

Goal: the optimizer is fully Form-native and witnessed, with no new runtime
meaning living in C lowering. The C seed may carry host install/call plumbing
while it shrinks, but this track treats Form recipes, Form emitters, and Form
receipts as the source of truth. Re-observed 2026-09-03: every cell named below
exists; a band with a number was re-run today; a band without one answers
nothing green today and is owed a heal.

## Invariants

- The optimizer proper is Form: decide, profile, specialize, lower, guard,
  deopt, melt, and witness.
- The walker remains the semantic oracle. Every native specialization needs a
  parity witness or a named pending receipt.
- Per-instance observations must collapse into stable numeric categories before
  they guide native code.
- A specialization must have a guard, fallback, and deopt/melt receipt.
- Form source must pass a static analyzer gate for facts that can be proven
  before execution or JIT lowering: missing source attribution, unbound symbols,
  arity mismatches, literal div/mod by zero, literal bounds faults, and static
  null/empty dereferences.
- A direct native access must preserve runtime fault semantics: bounds checks,
  null/nothing checks, div/mod-by-zero checks, type/shape checks, and structured
  exceptions with stack trace plus file/line/column/span attribution.
- Container access is not claimed direct unless the representation receipt proves
  the access path: cons head/tail, indexed buffer/vector, dict/hash bucket, or
  ordered tree path.
- CPU/GPU register wins are claims only after a Form emitter/witness names the
  register lane, spill/rooting behavior, and parity result.
- Numeric tags that cross JIT cells have one Form name at their first owner;
  container operation tags live in `model/jit-container-lowering.fk`.
- There is no flatten prerequisite and no static operations table: the native
  path for a recipe is generated from the recipe itself on demand
  (`form-agent-active-contribution.md`).

## What runs today — crystallize on heat

The live JIT is the heat lane: `observe/jit-evaluator-heat.fk` (band
`observe/tests/jit-evaluator-heat-band.fk` 4095) counts heat on the evaluator's
leaves, `form/form-stdlib/jit-heat-gate.fk` (band
`form/form-stdlib/tests/jit-heat-gate-band.fk` 4095) decides what crystallizes,
hot leaves crystallize native and melt on cool, and `observe/lane-counsel-run.fk`
(rows in `form/form-stdlib/lane-counsel.bml`, band 2047) judges the performance
lanes worst-first and names each lane's stone. The Metal lane emits every
pipeline from Form at runtime (`form-cli-mlx-band`'s prelude is owed by the twins
release; `jit-metal-lanes-band` 8191, `metal-handle-door-band` 65535).

## The policy spine (Form, witnessed)

- Profile receipt shape and numeric category collapse —
  `observe/jit-profile-receipt.fk` (`observe/tests/jit-profile-receipt-band.fk`):
  per-instance receipts collapse to category signatures; masks name crystallize,
  inline, stack, field, index, hash, tree, CPU, and GPU eligibility.
- Category-fed tiering — `observe/jit-tier-policy.fk`
  (`observe/tests/jit-tier-policy-band.fk`): receipts choose baseline/profile,
  hold, crystallize, specialize, deopt, or melt.
- Runtime checks and source-attributed exceptions — `observe/jit-runtime-fault.fk`
  (`observe/tests/jit-runtime-fault-band.fk` 511): bounds, null-ref, div/mod by
  zero, type/shape, and parity-checkable exception receipts with stack trace and
  full source attribution.
- Inlining and call tracking — `observe/jit-inline-policy.fk`
  (`observe/tests/jit-inline-policy-band.fk`): monomorphic calls inline,
  low-polymorphic calls need a guarded inline, megamorphic calls fall back.
- Static analyzer pre-execution gate — `observe/form-static-analyzer.fk`
  (`observe/tests/form-static-analyzer-band.fk`).
- Stack and frame collapse — `observe/jit-stack-frame.fk`
  (`observe/tests/jit-stack-frame-band.fk`).
- Representation specialization (field, array/list, dict/hashmap, ordered map) —
  `observe/jit-representation-specialization.fk`
  (`observe/tests/jit-representation-specialization-band.fk`).
- CPU register / SIMD and GPU register / memory lowering —
  `observe/jit-register-lowering.fk` (`observe/tests/jit-register-lowering-band.fk`).
- Deopt, melt, invalidation, and code cache — `observe/jit-deopt-cache.fk`
  (`observe/tests/jit-deopt-cache-band.fk`); the grouped sweep
  `observe/tests/jit-policy-front-sweep-band.fk`.
- Emitter bundle, native IR, host dispatch, backend emission, loader contract —
  `observe/jit-emitter-bundle.fk`, `observe/jit-native-ir.fk`,
  `observe/jit-host-dispatch.fk`, `observe/jit-backend-emission.fk`,
  `observe/jit-loader-contract.fk`, each with its `observe/tests/<name>-band.fk`.
- Native dispatch and witness sweeps — `observe/jit-native-dispatch-sweep.fk`,
  `observe/jit-full-track-sweep.fk`, `observe/jit-native-witness-sweep.fk`,
  `observe/jit-self-host-completion-sweep.fk`, `observe/jit-runtime-stack-attribution.fk`.

## The dylib bridge (the intended live-execution path)

Form still owns the JIT semantics — source lowering, container byte payloads,
guards, exception/deopt/melt/parity routes, generation, source maps — and the
host carrier may be treated as a callable native path only after all of them pass:

- `observe/jit-dylib-cache-lifecycle.fk` — `observe/tests/jit-dylib-cache-lifecycle-band.fk` 16777215
- `observe/jit-dylib-call-dispatch-evidence.fk` — band 134217727
- `observe/jit-dylib-call-result-evidence.fk` — band 134217727
- `observe/jit-dylib-invoke-return-evidence.fk` — band 268435455
- `observe/jit-dylib-live-proof-suite.fk` — band 536870911
- `observe/tests/jit-dylib-live-runtime-proof-band.fk` — 4294967295
- `observe/jit-rung20-dylib-runtime-audit.fk` — band 268435455
- `model/jit-source-runtime-orchestrator.fk` — `model/tests/jit-source-runtime-orchestrator-band.fk` 1048575
- the container pipeline — `model/jit-container-lowering.fk`, `-backend.fk`,
  `-byteplan.fk`, `-loader.fk`, `-source-runtime.fk`, `-profile-runtime.fk`,
  `-replacement-runtime.fk`, `-live-slot-runtime.fk`,
  `model/jit-source-dylib-container-executor.fk`,
  `model/jit-self-host-container-runtime-loop.fk`,
  `model/jit-self-host-container-live-evidence.fk`, each with its `model/tests/<name>-band.fk`
- the live bridge and gates — `observe/jit-source-replacement-runtime.fk`,
  `observe/jit-final-native-gate.fk`, `observe/jit-live-execution-evidence.fk`,
  `observe/jit-live-runtime-integration.fk`, `observe/jit-rung20-readiness.fk`,
  `observe/jit-host-membrane-current-gate.fk`,
  `observe/jit-dylib-live-runtime-container-gate.fk`,
  `observe/jit-slot-runtime-fault-bridge.fk`
- the POSIX W^X carrier repair lives in `runtime/fkwu-uni.c` (the seed's install
  path; a shrink candidate like the rest of the seed).

The fresh source front door already selects a fresh `.dylib` when a callable
native artifact exists (`HOMECOMING.md`).

## The last rung — pending

Full Form-native JIT witnessed: hot source recipes lower through the Form-owned
IR / backend bundles / byte streams into the existing host install/call membrane,
dispatch native, throw source-attributed runtime exceptions, deopt/melt safely,
and pass the repo's native witness sweep — without C-lowering as the optimizer
source. Rung 20's readiness audit (`observe/jit-rung20-readiness.fk`) composes
only current receipts; stale pre-container ones reject before it can compose.

## Owed heals

Most of the policy-spine bands above answer nothing green today (several stop
mid-form: `[input-ended-mid-form]`), and the string family is the hottest
uncovered lowering (`release-ledger.bml` R10). `observe/tree-heal.fk` is the
response to a broken cell, not a paragraph about it.
